Op 03-05-2023 om 09:21 schreef Erik van Oosten:
> Hi Philip,
>
>> Firstly, could you explain the situation
>> in that you would prefer to invoke commitAsync over commitSync in the
>> rebalance listener?
>
> Of course!
>
> Short answer: we prefer commitAsync because we want to handle multiple=20
> partitions concurrently using the ZIO runtime.
>
> Long answer: this is in the context of zio-kafka. In zio-kafka the=20
> user writes code for a stream that processes data and does commits. In=20
> the library we intercept those commits and pass them to the=20
> KafkaConsumer. We also keep track of the offsets of handed out=20
> records. Together this information allows us to track when a stream is=20
> ready processing a partition and that it is safe to start the rebalance=
.
>
> All of this happens concurrently and asynchronously using the ZIO=20
> runtime. When calling commit inside the onPartitionRevoked callback=20
> the library does a thread-id check; we can only call the KafkaConsumer=20
> from the same thread that invoked us. This is unfortunate because it=20
> forces us to spin up a specialized single-threaded ZIO runtime inside=20
> the callback method. Though this runtime can run blocking methods like=20
> commitSync, it will need careful programming since all other tasks=20
> need to wait.
>
> (BTW, it would be great if there is an option to disable the thread-id=20
> check. It has more use cases, see for example KAFKA-7143.)
>
>> is it your concern that we
>> currently don't have a way to invoke the callback, and the user won't=20
>> be to
>> correctly handle these failed/successful async commits?
>
> Yes, that is correct.
>
>> Sorry - I dug a bit into the old PR. Seems like the issue is there's=20
>> broken
>> contract that if the commitSync won't wait for the previous async=20
>> commits
>> to complete if it tries to commit an empty offset map.
>
> Indeed! I am assuming the same is true for commitAsync. The important=20
> thing is that we need something to get those callbacks. I would prefer=20
> commitAsync but if only commitSync gets fixed we can use that as well.=20
> If there is another method completely for this task, that would be=20
> good as well.
>
> Kind regards,
> =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 Erik.
>
>
> Philip Nee schreef op 2023-05-02 21:49:
>> Hey Erik,
>>
>> Just a couple of questions to you: Firstly, could you explain the=20
