Here is Tom Lee's PR recreated on trunk:=20
https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/13678

I believe that this PR might not be complete though. When we only call=20
commitAsync (repeatedly) from the rebalance listener callback method.=20
Will the client's poll method ever be invoked? I suspect that no polling=20
takes place in this scenario and that async commits will still not=20
complete. With the changes of this PR, commitSync can be used as a=20
workaround.

I guess we can fix this by adding `client.pollNoWakeup()`, e.g. at the=20
start of `ConsumerCoordinator.commitOffsetsAsync`. Is that an acceptable=20
change?

Kind regards,
 =C2=A0=C2=A0=C2=A0 Erik.


