nd
> > decided to elect C as the new leader
> > - 7. Before leader-election is performed, B replicates offset=3D1,2 fro=
m A.
> > offset=3D2 is committed
> >     * This is possible because even if A lost ZK session, A could handl=
e
> > fetch requests for a while.
> > - 8. Controller elects C as the new leader. B truncates its offset.
