om> wrote:
>
> Thanks for providing answers to my suggestions folks.
>
> Based on your answers, it seems like the KIP wants to do, relative durati=
on
> =3D (now - timestamp), where "now" is in UTC (and not in your machine's
> locale/timezone). Perhaps, it's worth clarifying in the KIP?
> Other than that, no more comments from my side. The proposal looks good t=
o
> me.
