    Resolution: Fixed

> Kafka Streams should support self-join on streams
> -------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-7497
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-7497
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: New Feature
>          Components: streams
>            Reporter: Robin Moffatt
>            Priority: Major
>              Labels: needs-kip
>
> There are valid reasons to want to join a stream to itself, but Kafka Str=
eams does not currently support this ({{Invalid topology: Topic foo has alr=
eady been registered by another source.}}).=C2=A0 To perform the join requi=
res creating a second stream as a clone of the first, and then doing a join=
 between the two. This is a clunky workaround and results in unnecessary du=
plication of data.



